 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“Amendment I. Congress shall make no law respecting an establishment of religion, or prohibiting the free exercise thereof; or abridging the freedom of speech, or of the press; or the right of the people peaceably to assemble, and to petition the government for a redress of grievances.</p>\n<p>Amendment II. A well regulated Militia, being necessary to the security of a free State, the right of the people to keep and bear Arms, shall not be infringed.</p>\n<p>Amendment III. No Soldier shall, in time of peace be quartered in any house, without the consent of the Owner, nor in time of war, but in a manner to be prescribed by law.”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">The United States Bill of Rights, 1789</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615000,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following pieces of outside evidence provides context for this document?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167973,
     "content_html": "Many citizens were concerned that individual rights were not expressed in the Constitution and demanded the addition."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167972,
     "content_html": "The Founders wanted to follow in the footsteps of Great Britain by adding a bill of rights."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167971,
     "content_html": "Women felt strongly their needs were not being met by the Constitution and held a convention of their own, resulting in this document."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167970,
     "content_html": "After intense debate, state conventions decided this document would replace the Constitution."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615001,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following did not influence the addition of the Bill of Rights?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167976,
     "content_html": "Actions taken by the British government before and during the Revolution inspired some of the amendments."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167975,
     "content_html": "State constitutions had articulated many of these rights prior to the Constitution."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167974,
     "content_html": "Political factions demanded clarification of inalienable rights to support the Constitution's ratification."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167977,
     "content_html": "The French alliance inspired the founders to adopt the French form of government."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615002,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which of the following explains why the amendments provided were not included in the original Constitution?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167981,
     "content_html": "State delegations at the Convention argued that additional amendments were unnecessary because most states already had a Bills of Rights."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167980,
     "content_html": "The Founders published the Constitution in newspapers and forgot to include the page with these amendments."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167979,
     "content_html": "The Founders were influenced by the British tradition of unwritten government that relied on precedent."
    },
    {
     "id": 1167978,
     "content_html": "Delegates at the convention were unable to reach a quorum to vote on these items, because the summer was over and many had already headed home."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615003,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which political faction primarily advocated the document excerpted previously?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1167984,
     "content_html": "Patriots"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167983,
     "content_html": "Loyalists"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167982,
     "content_html": "Federalists"
    },
    {
     "id": 1167985,
     "content_html": "Anti-Federalists"
    }
   ],
